{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge","id":1499730,"title":"Marcus Vitel's Sheriff and Scourge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-15T02:07:41-08:00","id":1499730,"title":"Marcus Vitel's Sheriff and Scourge","content":"I don't know if it's something obvious I'm missing, but I recently decided to reread D.C. By Night and can't find information on who is D.C's Sheriff, Scourge etc. Does anybody here have this information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T05:22:56-08:00","id":1499738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge#post1499730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's something obvious I'm missing, but I recently decided to reread D.C. By Night and can't find information on who is D.C's Sheriff, Scourge etc. Does anybody here have this information?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every Domain has to work in exactly the same ways and have the same positions. It's clear that DCbN's Vitel is an autocrat that doesn't hand out positions or grant honours. He has enforcers, but they work ad hoc instead of holding official titles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T06:26:18-08:00","id":1499744,"title":"","content":"I wonder of the age of the book has anything to do with there being no title &quot;Sheriff&quot; or &quot;Scourge.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know there a few books that don't have primogen councils, at least in name, because they where just old enough to not have that kind of title made for them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T09:04:10-08:00","id":1499759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499744#post1499744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder of the age of the book has anything to do with there being no title &quot;Sheriff&quot; or &quot;Scourge.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know there a few books that don't have primogen councils, at least in name, because they where just old enough to not have that kind of title made for them yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both a Primogen Council and a Sheriff appear in the 1st city module, Chicago by Night. The point is that they were supposed to be a feature of that city, no universal positions to be had at every city. Other cities that were released later had different structures, with only the Prince as a common feature. For example in Denver (Alien Hunger) the Prince is in a Triumvirate with a hidden elder and his Childe. The Prince of Cleveland (Blood Nativity) has 4 Lieutenants. In Milwaukee (Milwaukee by Night) there is a Council (actually the 1st to present the one per Clan idea, because in Chicago there are 2 Brujah but no Malkavian or Ventrue); there is no Sheriff, though, but the Anubi, a institution that fights the werewolves and, as an aside, helps to keep order. <br /> At some point the developers started getting unimaginative and tried to shoehorn a series of standard positions in every city, regardless of its personality. <br /> I still like to keep the original style, and for my Chicago+Midwest by Night game I have developed different Domain structures. It's quite refreshing to watch the PC's having to deal with different situations as they arrive, instead of just already having a fixed idea of what to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T10:17:50-08:00","id":1499763,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27429\" data-vbnamecard=\"27429\">Microcuchon</a> <br /> <br /> So lets talk about some things here because I think its important to have reference There is no Primogen Councils in Milwaukee, there is a 'Council of Elders that control the city' but the term &quot;Primogen Council' doesn't get used. Likewise Milwaukee has no 'Sheriff' by the role gets filled with the 'Anubi'. This is what I mean by <b>'at least in name'</b> because terms for things where not finalized for what things where. Like in the same Milwaukee book they talk about werewolves from the 'Mouse tribe' stuff wasn't so solid.<br /> <br /> Like wise lets talk about 'The Primogen' the coterie in Chicago. In the book it talks a bit about the coterie, &quot;The Primogen is the most powerful <b>Coterie</b> in they city. While most cities have no more then <b>three to five</b> Elders, Chicago has six, <b>more then any other city</b> in America. While this size can be (and often is) attributed to the fact that the Chicago metropolitan area is the third largest in the United States and the largest under direct Camarilla control, blame really lies with the <b>Methuselahs</b>. At least two of the Primogen are direct decendents from one or the other, and most of the others have spent a good deal of time under their subtle Domination.&quot;<br /> <br /> So that is the first paragraph, emphasis mine. Its clear to me that the idea of 'a council of elder vampires' was in a very primordial state that, again, the ideas of these roles are there but its not in the shape we would recognize as 'a primogen council.' I bring this up because the roles of &quot;Sheriff&quot; and &quot;Scourge&quot; are probably in the book but not called &quot;Sheriff&quot; and &quot;Scourge.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T12:55:02-08:00","id":1499776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I bring this up because the roles of &quot;Sheriff&quot; and &quot;Scourge&quot; are probably in the book but not called &quot;Sheriff&quot; and &quot;Scourge.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I was thinking when I started the discussion. The thing is, I still couldn't find who's responsible for these roles in the city. Cities can vary a lot in the way they function, but the roles are usually easy to identify. As we can see looking at the aforementioned Anubi in Milwaukee's case. My problem here is that I still couldn't find anyone who is responsible for these roles in Washington D.C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T13:00:36-08:00","id":1499779,"title":"","content":"The standardization of a domain's &quot;court&quot; really came about because of LARP. The Mind's Eye books seemed to cement in everyone's mind that a domain always had certain positions (that PCs could fill) and that the Primogen had one representative for each clan (that PCs could fill). But that was not how the actual city sourcebooks described it.<br /> <br /> Obviously you could backfill in some positions. Neally would have been Lodin's Seneschal even though he was not called as such. &quot;Sheriff&quot; would of course be the Sheriff. Many of the &quot;elders&quot; mentioned in the Coterie section would in fact be the Harpies. But positions like Scourge or Keeper of Elysium did not seem to exist.<br /> <br /> Early books would mention the Primogen and Harpies, but otherwise each Prince seemed to decide for himself what kind of henchmen he needed to get things done.<br /> <br /> An interesting thing about Chicago's Primogen Council is that it showed Primogen were not about clans, but about powerful individuals. The Ventrue clan, despite ostensibly being the single most powerful clan in all of Chicago, did not have anyone on the Primogen Council. Although there were adventures about Ballard hoping to become one. There were two Brujah on the Council, and one interpretation of the domain's history implied there might have been three Brujah (when Procet was around).<br /> <br /> So many of the things players &quot;know&quot; from LARP/Revised that cemented certain positions in the Revised era going forward actually did not exist in the original game.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> Besides ignoring the actual name for the position, all a Seneschal is someone who handles routine administrative tasks for the Prince. All a Sheriff is someone who is willing to get her knuckles bruised being the muscle for the Prince in order to enforce his rules. So the question of who is the Seneschal or Sheriff of Marcus Vitel in DC by Night is who, if anyone, performed these tasks?<br /> <br /> I believe this is best answered by the coterie charts, particularly the section called The Prince's Allies.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue Gino Martinelli handles a lot of things that would often be done by a Seneschal, but is mainly limited to influence matters of mortal law enforcement and the underworld. His childe Karina Dobson also does some of this work, as she arranges political matters with Kindred in other domains. We also know that Vitel's childe Monica Black is mentioned to be &quot;second only to the Prince.&quot; She's also one of the Harpies and has extensive influence among the lobbyists and legal fraternity. I would say that the Seneschal position is probably split between them. Monica probably handles a lot of Vitel's interaction with Kindred, seemingly on an informal basis; while Gino does a lot of the actual work managing the city through mortals.<br /> <br /> In terms of enforcers, we're told that Marcus prefers to utilize up and coming neonates by giving them tasks to do and areas to control, but subsequently undermining them but offering to forgive them if they blood bond themselves to him. I say collectively these Kindred make up the Sheriff, at least in terms of how the Camarilla sees it. Marcus manages these (unnamed and unmentioned coterie) Kindred, but they do the dirty work of enforcing things. Secretly there is also the Ventrue Karin Dobson who does Marcus's intelligence gathering and controls a team of Delta Force trained ghouls who can eliminate people. Of course, Marcus' &quot;real&quot; &quot;Sheriff&quot; and &quot;Scourge&quot; is the Sabbat Jack whom he uses to destroy Kindred he wants eliminated. I believe that most of the DC Camarilla understands that Marcus has a variety of Kindred acting in the &quot;Sheriff&quot; role, but nobody knows the extent of it or who does what.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel likes to delegate a lot of work, but he prefers to work with a dispersed crowd and not concentrate power in his subordinates. He doesn't get his hands dirty himself, but he certainly makes a lot of arrangements with the Kindred who do. That has to keep the many very busy.<br /> <br /> If I didn't want to reveal to the PCs (and NPC Kindred) how Vitel actually operates, and present something that seems to match the &quot;standard&quot; roles, I would tell people that Monica acts as his Seneschal and Gino as his Sheriff. But then let the PCs figure out for themselves that they don't seem to actually do all the duties they would assume, and that there are plenty of other people doing bits of each role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T15:58:49-08:00","id":1499794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499779#post1499779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The standardization of a domain's &quot;court&quot; really came about because of LARP. The Mind's Eye books seemed to cement in everyone's mind that a domain always had certain positions (that PCs could fill) and that the Primogen had one representative for each clan (that PCs could fill). But that was not how the actual city sourcebooks described it.<br /> <br /> Obviously you could backfill in some positions. Neally would have been Lodin's Seneschal even though he was not called as such. &quot;Sheriff&quot; would of course be the Sheriff. Many of the &quot;elders&quot; mentioned in the Coterie section would in fact be the Harpies. But positions like Scourge or Keeper of Elysium did not seem to exist.<br /> <br /> Early books would mention the Primogen and Harpies, but otherwise each Prince seemed to decide for himself what kind of henchmen he needed to get things done.<br /> <br /> An interesting thing about Chicago's Primogen Council is that it showed Primogen were not about clans, but about powerful individuals. The Ventrue clan, despite ostensibly being the single most powerful clan in all of Chicago, did not have anyone on the Primogen Council. Although there were adventures about Ballard hoping to become one. There were two Brujah on the Council, and one interpretation of the domain's history implied there might have been three Brujah (when Procet was around).<br /> <br /> So many of the things players &quot;know&quot; from LARP/Revised that cemented certain positions in the Revised era going forward actually did not exist in the original game.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> Besides ignoring the actual name for the position, all a Seneschal is someone who handles routine administrative tasks for the Prince. All a Sheriff is someone who is willing to get her knuckles bruised being the muscle for the Prince in order to enforce his rules. So the question of who is the Seneschal or Sheriff of Marcus Vitel in DC by Night is who, if anyone, performed these tasks?<br /> <br /> I believe this is best answered by the coterie charts, particularly the section called The Prince's Allies.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue Gino Martinelli handles a lot of things that would often be done by a Seneschal, but is mainly limited to influence matters of mortal law enforcement and the underworld. His childe Karina Dobson also does some of this work, as she arranges political matters with Kindred in other domains. We also know that Vitel's childe Monica Black is mentioned to be &quot;second only to the Prince.&quot; She's also one of the Harpies and has extensive influence among the lobbyists and legal fraternity. I would say that the Seneschal position is probably split between them. Monica probably handles a lot of Vitel's interaction with Kindred, seemingly on an informal basis; while Gino does a lot of the actual work managing the city through mortals.<br /> <br /> In terms of enforcers, we're told that Marcus prefers to utilize up and coming neonates by giving them tasks to do and areas to control, but subsequently undermining them but offering to forgive them if they blood bond themselves to him. I say collectively these Kindred make up the Sheriff, at least in terms of how the Camarilla sees it. Marcus manages these (unnamed and unmentioned coterie) Kindred, but they do the dirty work of enforcing things. Secretly there is also the Ventrue Karin Dobson who does Marcus's intelligence gathering and controls a team of Delta Force trained ghouls who can eliminate people. Of course, Marcus' &quot;real&quot; &quot;Sheriff&quot; and &quot;Scourge&quot; is the Sabbat Jack whom he uses to destroy Kindred he wants eliminated. I believe that most of the DC Camarilla understands that Marcus has a variety of Kindred acting in the &quot;Sheriff&quot; role, but nobody knows the extent of it or who does what.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel likes to delegate a lot of work, but he prefers to work with a dispersed crowd and not concentrate power in his subordinates. He doesn't get his hands dirty himself, but he certainly makes a lot of arrangements with the Kindred who do. That has to keep the many very busy.<br /> <br /> If I didn't want to reveal to the PCs (and NPC Kindred) how Vitel actually operates, and present something that seems to match the &quot;standard&quot; roles, I would tell people that Monica acts as his Seneschal and Gino as his Sheriff. But then let the PCs figure out for themselves that they don't seem to actually do all the duties they would assume, and that there are plenty of other people doing bits of each role.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you very much for the long and detailed response. It seems, as I thought at first, the city doesn't have anyone actually responsible for these roles. Not officially at least, but rather many cainites who could act in ways fitting these roles. I'm thinking about using Vitel in a story taking place much before the D.C by Night, so I wanted to &quot;import&quot; some characters in order to build my scenario (and save at least some work), so I thought about who else could be with Vitel in the city, acting in some of the traditional roles cainites act in a city. It seems I'm probably going to have a lot more work than anticipated as I'll have to come up with more characters than expected. There aren't many that could be easily &quot;imported&quot; from D.C. Besides Jack, naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T18:04:31-08:00","id":1499810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499763#post1499763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> So lets talk about some things here because I think its important to have reference There is no Primogen Councils in Milwaukee, there is a 'Council of Elders that control the city' but the term &amp;quot;Primogen Council' doesn't get used. Likewise Milwaukee has no 'Sheriff' by the role gets filled with the 'Anubi'. This is what I mean by <b>'at least in name'</b> because terms for things where not finalized for what things where. Like in the same Milwaukee book they talk about werewolves from the 'Mouse tribe' stuff wasn't so solid.<br /> <br /> Like wise lets talk about 'The Primogen' the coterie in Chicago. In the book it talks a bit about the coterie, &amp;quot;The Primogen is the most powerful <b>Coterie</b> in they city. While most cities have no more then <b>three to five</b> Elders, Chicago has six, <b>more then any other city</b> in America. While this size can be (and often is) attributed to the fact that the Chicago metropolitan area is the third largest in the United States and the largest under direct Camarilla control, blame really lies with the <b>Methuselahs</b>. At least two of the Primogen are direct decendents from one or the other, and most of the others have spent a good deal of time under their subtle Domination.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So that is the first paragraph, emphasis mine. Its clear to me that the idea of 'a council of elder vampires' was in a very primordial state that, again, the ideas of these roles are there but its not in the shape we would recognize as 'a primogen council.' I bring this up because the roles of &amp;quot;Sheriff&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Scourge&amp;quot; are probably in the book but not called &amp;quot;Sheriff&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Scourge.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But as @Blsck Fox explained, it wasn't only that they lacked the names, it's that certain positions didn't exist. The Scourge is the clearest example, because it was a role introduced together with the thin bloods. There were no thin bloods during 1st and early 2nd edition, so there is no scourge in any of these books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T21:14:00-08:00","id":1499828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499810#post1499810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But as @Blsck Fox explained, it wasn't only that they lacked the names, it's that certain positions didn't exist. The Scourge is the clearest example, because it was a role introduced together with the thin bloods. There were no thin bloods during 1st and early 2nd edition, so there is no scourge in any of these books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps not in name, but a &quot;Sheriff&quot; has always existed in a form or another, also a Scourge's role is much more than getting rid of disgusting thin bloods, but basically any undesirable in the Prince's domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T02:02:32-08:00","id":1499849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499828#post1499828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps not in name, but a &quot;Sheriff&quot; has always existed in a form or another, also a Scourge's role is much more than getting rid of disgusting thin bloods, but basically any undesirable in the Prince's domain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth be told, i'd say the concepts of sheriff, scourge or hound have far from insignificant overlap, in different degrees all serving together the general role of &quot;prince's thugboy squad&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> That as an aside, in Milwaukee back then i'd say this function was played (unofficially) more by Turk and the Union anarch gang than the Anubi, who were pretty much mono-focused into lupine-hunting with Decker seen as a <i>rogue </i>member of the Council, until memetic mutation and Gangrel: Revised considerably changed things. But there was a clear undercurrent that the Caitiff gang leader was the Milwaukee's Juggler/Sheriff, the troublemaker that made deals with the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-20-2023, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T04:32:55-08:00","id":1499851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499849#post1499849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Truth be told, i'd say the concepts of sheriff, scourge or hound have far from insignificant overlap, in different degrees all serving together the general role of &amp;quot;prince's thugboy squad&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> That as an aside, in Milwaukee back then i'd say this function was played (unofficially) more by Turk and the Union anarch gang than the Anubi, who were pretty much mono-focused into lupine-hunting with Decker seem as a <i>rogue </i>member of the Council, until memetic mutation and Gangrel: Revised considerably changed things. But there was a clear undercurrent that the Caitiff gang leader was the Milwaukee's Juggler/Sheriff, the troublemaker that made deals with the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with that take. Considering the fact that Turk was officially an Anarch and his control by the Prince a secret, this is one more argument for the &quot;each Domain is ruled in completely different ways&quot; idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T10:28:16-08:00","id":1499867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499810#post1499810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But as @Blsck Fox explained, it wasn't only that they lacked the names, it's that certain positions didn't exist. The Scourge is the clearest example, because it was a role introduced together with the thin bloods. There were no thin bloods during 1st and early 2nd edition, so there is no scourge in any of these books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why you are tagging me to say this, when it's what I said.<br /> <br /> &quot;the ideas of these roles are there but its not in the shape we would recognize&quot;<br /> &quot;I wonder of the age of the book has anything to do with there being no title &quot;Sheriff&quot; or &quot;Scourge.&quot;&quot;<br /> &quot;because they where just old enough to not have that kind of title made for them yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do not cite the Deep Magic to me. I was there when it was written","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T10:31:33-08:00","id":1499868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Truth be told, i'd say the concepts of sheriff, scourge or hound have far from insignificant overlap, in different degrees all serving together the general role of &quot;prince's thugboy squad&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Yes, truth be told, I've always felt there was overlap in their roles, in any case, here I was exactly more interested in knowing Vitel's &quot;thugboy squad&quot; as you put it. Because as you see he doesn't trust Monica or Cynthia (not that his daughters could help much in this situation in any case), so I'm curious to know who are the men he really trust to help him keep order in town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T12:00:02-08:00","id":1499875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499849#post1499849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That as an aside, in Milwaukee back then i'd say this function was played (unofficially) more by Turk and the Union anarch gang than the Anubi</div> </div> </div> </div>Milwaukee is a very strange case. It's said that Hrothulf was the original Prince, but when he stepped down he gave domain to the Council of Elders who appointed the next Prince(s). But while the Prince runs the city and administers the Traditions, it seems like it is the Council (collectively) rather than the Prince who holds domain. It seems to have a lot more formal powers (and be formally organized) than the the traditional Primogen. If I was running a chronicle using MbN, I'd interpret this to mean while the Prince has all the formal powers of Prince that the Council could decide to veto a decision or command the Prince to take a specific action based on a majority of the Council votes.<br /> <br /> As for who would be Terence Merik's &quot;Sheriff&quot;, my reading of the book is that Merik used several people to enforce his commands - himself (he has some good combat stats and has a Celerity + Protean 2 (Wolf Claws) combination of Disciplines), his ghouls and mortals, and secret use of Lupines to kill people through his Gangrel &quot;wife's&quot; connections with the Lupines. These were Lupines in a &quot;Mouse&quot; pack, but given that this is an early product that does not match the later Werewolf setting we would need to make appropriate revisions. I'd probably make them some kind of Bone Gnawer pack under Rat who had personal reasons to be allies with a fairly humane Gangrel. His use of the Lupines to secretly eliminate his enemies would have ended once his wife was destroyed, so it makes sense that he would create &quot;the Mask&quot; as replacement agents and &quot;the Mask&quot; (aka the PCs) in Psychomachia essentially fulfill the role of a sheriff. Combined with his Domination of Turk and the Union, he did a good job of keeping his enemies divided. And of course Decker and the Anubi were freely providing their services to keep the domain safe from the Lupines in general which would normally be something a Prince would handle. To outsiders, it'd look like Merik was his own enforcer and was very good at using divide &amp; conquer tactics. But he was getting a LOT of help even though it didn't look like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T14:57:54-08:00","id":1499911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499875#post1499875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Milwaukee is a very strange case. It's said that Hrothulf was the original Prince, but when he stepped down he gave domain to the Council of Elders who appointed the next Prince(s). But while the Prince runs the city and administers the Traditions, it seems like it is the Council (collectively) rather than the Prince who holds domain. It seems to have a lot more formal powers (and be formally organized) than the the traditional Primogen. If I was running a chronicle using MbN, I'd interpret this to mean while the Prince has all the formal powers of Prince that the Council could decide to veto a decision or command the Prince to take a specific action based on a majority of the Council votes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, the Council, its workings and actual degree of power/representation is a convoluted mess - and truth be told, i always saw it as premeditated as, gothic antihero pretensions notwithstanding, Hrothulf is a 1600+ years old undead monster with (partly justified) paranoia and persecution mania.<br /> <br /> The prince offers power and recognition as a primogen in all but name, more even, since an active council can be expected to pick/support a new prince in case of the previous retirement (as with Hrothulf) or destruction (in Merrik and at least one of his precursors' case) - except for the little fact its official role and format makes it so you'll have those elders constantly butting heads and distracted with power or point of view disputes between each other. Don't you think it's an <i>incredible coincidence</i> that Decker's position was pulled out instead of a replacement picked, leaving the Council at 6 in number, a situation where <i><b>any </b></i>dispute can lead to a dealock, and dependent on the prince's intervention to act as tie-breaker?<br /> <br /> Not to mention their purported clan representation role implies that clanmates that feel unrepresented could band together to either protest with the prince or bring the councilor down &quot;for the sake of clan interests&quot;, meaning that every councilor has to look over his shoulder and make sure to attend to the interests of its clanmates to some degree. So, the great power of the Clan Council <b>on paper</b> can be seen as a major resource but also point of dissention and conflict purposefully built-in by Hrothulf to minimize threats against his own person and that Merrik would exploit in his own preservation of praxis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499730-marcus-vitel-s-sheriff-and-scourge?p=1499875#post1499875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for who would be Terence Merik's &quot;Sheriff&quot;, my reading of the book is that Merik used several people to enforce his commands - himself (he has some good combat stats and has a Celerity + Protean 2 (Wolf Claws) combination of Disciplines), his ghouls and mortals, and secret use of Lupines to kill people through his Gangrel &quot;wife's&quot; connections with the Lupines. These were Lupines in a &quot;Mouse&quot; pack, but given that this is an early product that does not match the later Werewolf setting we would need to make appropriate revisions. I'd probably make them some kind of Bone Gnawer pack under Rat who had personal reasons to be allies with a fairly humane Gangrel. His use of the Lupines to secretly eliminate his enemies would have ended once his wife was destroyed, so it makes sense that he would create &quot;the Mask&quot; as replacement agents and &quot;the Mask&quot; (aka the PCs) in Psychomachia essentially fulfill the role of a sheriff. Combined with his Domination of Turk and the Union, he did a good job of keeping his enemies divided. And of course Decker and the Anubi were freely providing their services to keep the domain safe from the Lupines in general which would normally be something a Prince would handle. To outsiders, it'd look like Merik was his own enforcer and was very good at using divide &amp; conquer tactics. But he was getting a LOT of help even though it didn't look like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that definitely fits with how things work in the book, not to mention Demitri, the crazed Nosferatu alchemist that apprently served as Merik's secret hatchet man too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-09-2023, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}